# tests/lookaround/quantified.rxt -- module `lookaround` ([M6.6.2] wave B+C): `(?=a)*` and family, including §2.6's empty-iteration cells
#
# GENERATED BY tests/lookaround/gen_corpus.py, and that is a property rather
# than a convenience. Every expectation below was produced by driving the cell
# through libpcre2 10.46 (the committed ctypes binding at
# docs/design/eng_brep_measurements/probes/pcre2_ctypes.py) BEFORE it was
# written, and python3 `re` was driven over the SAME cells in the same pass; a
# block carries `# pcre2-only` exactly where python diverged or could not
# compile the pattern -- DETECTED, never assumed, with the first divergence and
# the cell count recorded above the marking. The generator never asks pcrec
# anything: an expectation derived from the compiler under test is not an
# expectation.
#
# WHY THE MARKING IS COMPUTED RATHER THAN DECLARED. Design §7 catalogues TWO
# expectations about this module that a hand-marking would have written in and
# that are REFUTED by measurement: python compiles all fourteen QUANTIFIED
# lookaround forms and agrees on all nine behavioural cells (G8), and the two
# oracles agree on all 27 CAPTURE cells including captures in a negative
# lookahead (G9). R32 C3 is the standing precedent -- a test plan that marked
# two files python-verifiable in the direction that LOSES the oracle.
#
# EVERY BLOCK NAMES `lookaround` IN ITS `features` LINE (R33 V-10): `std1` is a
# FROZEN named set, {classes, modifiers}, so it does not contain this module,
# and a corpus cell that forgot the feature would pass by REFUSAL -- S108's
# masking shape applied to a whole file.
#
# Design: docs/design/lookaround_design.md.


# THE EMPTY-ITERATION CELL, and it is here because it must TERMINATE. A
# lookaround consumes nothing on every path, so `vm_nullable` MUST answer
# true for it or the star loses its empty-iteration guard. The failure is NOT
# a hang: every VM artifact carries a step budget, so the lost guard BURNS it
# and returns PCREC_ERR_STEPS. Sabotage row S125, whose detector has to
# notice an ERROR return.
pattern ^(?=a)*a$
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1
n "b"

# The same, one group deeper.
pattern ^(?:(?=a))*a$
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1

# The same with a CONSUMING alternative beside the zero-width one.
pattern ^(?:(?=a)|b)*a$
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1
m "ba" 0 2

# The same for the NEGATIVE form, whose body-failed frame is what the
# iteration keeps re-pushing.
pattern ^(?:(?!x))*a$
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1
n "x"

# The same with a CAPTURE inside, so the guard and the trail interact.
pattern ^(?:(?=(a)))*a$
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1
g 1 0 1

# §2.6: quantified lookaround SHIPS -- all fourteen forms compile in BOTH
# oracles, which REFUTES the charter's expectation that python lacks it
# (design §7, G8). Marking these `# pcre2-only` would have thrown a working
# oracle away.
pattern (?=a)*a
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1
m "ba" 1 2

pattern (?=a)+a
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1
n "b"

pattern (?=a)?a
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1
n "b"

pattern (?=a){2}a
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1

pattern (?=a){0,3}a
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1

pattern (?!a)?b
features lookaround
m "b" 0 1
m "ab" 1 2

pattern (?!a)*b
features lookaround
m "b" 0 1

# The POSSESSIVE spelling, which desugars to `A_ATOMIC(A_REP(A_LOOK))` -- a
# cut ABOVE an assertion that has a cut of its own.
pattern (?=a)*+a
features lookaround,atomic-groups
m "a" 0 1

# The LAZY spelling.
pattern (?=a)*?a
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1

# A quantified assertion inside a CAPTURE: the group spans the empty run of
# iterations.
pattern ((?=a)*)a
features lookaround
m "a" 0 1
g 1 0 0

# An assertion inside a CONSUMING loop -- the iteration is not empty, so this
# exercises the ordinary rung with the marks re-set per pass.
pattern (?:(?=a)a)+
features lookaround
m "aa" 0 2
m "ab" 0 1
